# OrkoPay — AI assistant context

## What this repo is

OrkoPay is OrkoNet's on-chain payment settlement layer. Customers pay checkout
invoices in ETH or USDC; the contract credits merchants net of the platform fee;
merchants withdraw to a registered payout address. A TypeScript indexer confirms
payments against invoices in Postgres.

Read `docs/architecture.md` first for the flow, accounting rules and trust model.

## Layout

- `src/OrkoPay.sol` — settlement (deposit, depositToken, refund, withdraw, collectFees)
- `src/OrkoPayRegistry.sol` — merchant directory (owner + operator roles)
- `src/libraries/` — FeeMath (bps math), SafeTransferLib (ETH/ERC-20 transfers)
- `src/utils/` — Ownable2Step, Pausable, ReentrancyGuard (adapted from OZ v5)
- `src/periphery/OrkoPayLens.sol` — read-only batch helper
- `test/` — Foundry tests; shared fixture in `test/utils/BaseTest.sol`
- `indexer/` — viem + pg service; handlers in `src/handlers.ts`

## Conventions

- `asset == address(0)` means native ETH everywhere.
- Checks-Effects-Interactions; `nonReentrant` on all value-moving functions.
- Fees in basis points via `FeeMath` only. `250 bps = 2.5%`.
- Typed custom errors from `IOrkoPay` / the relevant contract; no require strings in `src/`.
- Modifier order: `external payable whenNotPaused nonReentrant`.
- NatSpec `@notice` on every public/external function; `@inheritdoc` for interface impls.
- Event signature changes must be mirrored in `indexer/src/abi.ts`.

## Commands

```bash
forge build
forge test
forge test --match-test test_<name> -vvv
forge test --match-path "test/invariant/*"
forge coverage
cd indexer && npm test && npm run typecheck
```

## Solidity version

`0.8.24`, EVM `cancun`. Do not change without updating `foundry.toml` and CI.
